From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:58:01 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: Add the Tensor G4 Hibern8 sequences

Google's UFS driver runs a PMA sequence after every Hibern8 entry
(ufs_cal_post_h8_enter) and another before every exit
(ufs_cal_pre_h8_exit). The Tensor G4 PHY data has no cfgs_hibern8, so
phy_notify_state() writes nothing and the PMA stays in its active
setting while the link is in Hibern8.

Add both tables from Google's zuma calibration, which the zuma and
zumapro builds share (CONFIG_SOC_ZUMA). After entry: the TRSV_SQ
registers 0x9f4 = 0x08 and 0xa00 = 0x3a on each lane, the common
register 0x000 = 0x51, then 0xb64 = 0x30 and 0x33 on each lane. Before
exit: 0x000 = 0x11, a 10 us wait, 0x9f4 = 0x00 and 0xa00 = 0x30, then
0xb64 = 0x32 and 0x22. As in the existing table, Google's byte offsets
are converted to words and the lane stride is 0x800 bytes. The
sequences are the same for every power mode (PMD_ALL), and Google's
exit sequence has no CDR wait, so no wait_for_cdr is needed.

As on gs101, the host driver runs the entry sequence after it has
stopped the host clocks, where Google's runs it just before.

The Pixel 8 Pro binds this data through its google,zuma-ufs-phy
fallback. Its host has no idle clock gating, and runtime PM of its
LUNs stays off unless userspace allows it, so it enters Hibern8 only
on the way to turning the link off, at shutdown and system suspend.
Google's driver runs the same entry sequence there, from the same
tables.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/ufs/zuma/ufs-cal.h
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-zumapro-ufs.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-zumapro-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-zumapro-ufs.c
index 899a327f5..195342435 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-zumapro-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-zumapro-ufs.c
@@ -56,10 +56,36 @@ static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg zumapro_pre_init[] = {
 	END_UFS_PHY_CFG,
 };
 
+/* Google's post_h8_enter: after the link has entered Hibern8. */
+static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg zumapro_post_h8_enter[] = {
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x27d, 0x08, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x280, 0x3a, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_COMN_REG_CFG(0x000, 0x51, PWR_MODE_ANY),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x2d9, 0x30, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x2d9, 0x33, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	END_UFS_PHY_CFG,
+};
+
+/* Google's pre_h8_exit: before the link leaves Hibern8. */
+static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg zumapro_pre_h8_exit[] = {
+	PHY_COMN_REG_CFG(0x000, 0x11, PWR_MODE_ANY),
+	PHY_DELAY_US_CFG(10),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x27d, 0x00, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x280, 0x30, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x2d9, 0x32, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(0x2d9, 0x22, PWR_MODE_ANY, 0x200),
+	END_UFS_PHY_CFG,
+};
+
 static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg *zumapro_cfgs[CFG_TAG_MAX] = {
 	[CFG_PRE_INIT] = zumapro_pre_init,
 };
 
+static const struct samsung_ufs_phy_cfg *zumapro_hibern8_cfgs[] = {
+	[CFG_POST_HIBERN8_ENTER]	= zumapro_post_h8_enter,
+	[CFG_PRE_HIBERN8_EXIT]		= zumapro_pre_h8_exit,
+};
+
 static const char * const zumapro_clks[] = { "ref_clk" };
 
 static int zumapro_wait_for_cal(struct phy *phy, u8 lane)
@@ -79,6 +105,7 @@ static int zumapro_wait_for_cal(struct phy *phy, u8 lane)
 
 const struct samsung_ufs_phy_drvdata tensor_zumapro_ufs_phy = {
 	.cfgs = zumapro_cfgs,
+	.cfgs_hibern8 = zumapro_hibern8_cfgs,
 	.isol = {
 		.offset = 0x3ec0,
 		.mask = BIT(0),
